uchi  in the face of brutal crackdowns on  dissent now  activists say the military junta is  weaponizing kovid 19  against its own people redmond shannon  reports  another clamber for oxygen during a  brutal rise in covet 19 cases  this time in myanmar allegedly made  worse by the military regime withholding  medical supplies from its opponents  healthcare workers are being attacked  and arrested  the virus is spreading through the  population  very fast indeed  on sunday leader minong yang blamed the  opposition for the virus spread  marking six months since his coup he is  promising  free and fair elections by august 2023  with two more years of a state of  emergency  if he actually believes in democracy  and democratic values he wouldn't stage  a coup  on fest of february and continue killing  civilians until today  so again these are empty promises  is a burmese democracy activist just  like her father  he was jailed at the start of the coup  months of protests since then have seen  hundreds of deaths  and thousands of arrests quintone says  the previous regime of aung sang tsuchi  was deeply flawed too accountable to the  military  but it was democratically elected in  burma we never had  a genuine or even a you know democracy  at all  in city areas yes we had a relative  freedom but in ethnic area  um human rights abuses and human rights  violations continue  in that 10 years period including the  persecution and killing of rohingya  muslims in 2017  actions ottawa calls genocide long-term  change  she says will need more international  pressure like the sanctions imposed by  canada  and others they have been able to get  away with  all these atrocities not from not only  from the 1st of february but from  many many decades and so they have this  sense of impunity that they can get away  with  almost everything leaders in the region  meet monday to appoint an  envoy to broker talks between the junta  and the opposition  and this week the first trial of su chi 